# Testing (ai-spector)

## Where tests live

- Root folder: `tests/` (not `src/`, not `__tests__/`)
- Mirror `src/` paths: `src/graph/Foo.ts` → `tests/graph/Foo.test.ts`
- Never add `*.test.ts` under `src/` — build output must stay test-free

## Naming and imports

- Suffix: `*.test.ts`
- Framework: Vitest (`describe`, `it`, `expect`)
- Import from `src` using relative paths + `.js` extension (Node16 ESM), e.g. `../../src/graph/InMemoryGraph.js`

## Running

- `npm test` — CI-style single run
- `npm run test:watch` — local watch
- `npm run build` — must still pass; only compiles `src/`

## What to write

- **Unit tests (default):** pure functions, graph logic, validators, transforms
- **Integration (sparingly):** `tests/integration/` for CLI or multi-file flows; use temp dirs and real fixtures
- Skip trivial Commander glue unless it encodes real behavior

## Mocking

- Prefer real data and small fixtures
- Mock external I/O only (`fs`, `child_process`, network)
- Do not mock the module under test

## After changes

Run `npm test` and `npm run build` before finishing. Full guide: `docs/testing.md`.
